 "exercise_notes": "Bloom levels and concept tags are AI-generated; every answer is the book’s except the suggested approaches marked as such. The 30 even-numbered section exercises have no answer in the book’s key. Exercise 406, showing a function is a probability density function, is kept with an AI-written suggested approach; exercise 405, whose key says only “Answers will vary,” has one too. The other 29 are computational and are left out: exercises 348–352 even and 356–372 even (evaluate or show divergence), 354 (convergence without integrating), 374–384 even (by comparison or directly), 386, 388, 390 and 392 (discontinuous integrands), 394, 396, 398 and 400 (areas and volumes), and 402 and 404 (Laplace transforms). Review exercises 427, 428 and 429 are held here; 428 and 429, proofs about the gamma function with no answer in the key, have AI-written suggested approaches. 426 and 430 have no answer in the key and are left out, and so is 431, whose key says only “Answers may vary” and which integrates the curve fitted in 430. The chapter’s other review exercises are held in the sections that teach what they test: 408 and 411 in 7.1, 413 and 419 in 7.3, 409, 415 and 421 in 7.4, 417 in 7.5, and 410, 423 and 425 in 7.6.",
