   "cite": "infinite",
   "prompt": "<p>A non-negative function is a probability density function if it satisfies the following definition: $\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}f(t)dt=1 .$ The probability that a random variable <em>x</em> lies between <em>a</em> and <em>b</em> is given by $P(a\\le x\\le b)=\\int_a^{b}f(t)dt .$</p><p>Show that $f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}0\\;\\text{if}\\;x\\lt 0 \\\\ 7e^{-7x}\\text{if}\\;x\\ge 0\\end{array}\\right.$ is a probability density function.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "solution": "The function is never negative, and $\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}f(t)dt=\\int_0^{\\infty}7e^{-7t}dt=\\lim_{b\\to \\infty}(-e^{-7t})\\Big|_0^{b}=\\lim_{b\\to \\infty}(1-e^{-7b})=1,$ so $f$ is a probability density function.",
    "generated_by": "ai"
   }
