    "solution": "Integrate by parts with $u=y^{a-1}$ and $dv=e^{-y}dy,$ so that $du=(a-1)y^{a-2}dy$ and $v=-e^{-y}:$ $\\Gamma (a)=\\lim_{t\\to \\infty}\\left[-y^{a-1}e^{-y}\\right]_0^{t}+(a-1)\\int_0^{\\infty}e^{-y}y^{a-2}dy.$ For $a\\gt 1$ the bracket is $0$ at both ends, since $e^{-y}$ shrinks faster than any power of $y$ grows, which leaves $\\Gamma (a)=(a-1)\\Gamma (a-1).$",
    "generated_by": "ai"
